    "notes": "Login is the same challenge family as TL-WR840N/WR841N but a different build of it: the issuer is /login?form=auth returning JSON {key:[nn,ee],seq}, the key is reported as k=<key>&i=<iv> (not key=/iv=), and sign/data travel as two ordinary form fields rather than a CRLF-framed body. The signature signs 53-byte chunks, which is 512-bit minus PKCS#1 v1.5's 11 bytes of padding -- the same k-11 rule with different chunk arithmetic.\n\nVerified without hardware the same way as the other two families: the firmware's own tpEncrypt.js, encrypt.js and cryptoJS.min.js were executed under Node with a fixed key/IV, and the Python port reproduced the MD5, the base64 ciphertext and the signed string byte for byte.\n\nNot verified: that a real C6 accepts it. No device was present."
